    "reasons": "The formalization has two major problems. First, the condition 'no two vectors are collinear' is encoded as ¬ Collinear ℝ {a,b} etc., but in Lean Collinear is affine collinearity of points. Any two points (including two vectors viewed as points in ℝ × ℝ) are always collinear, so these negated conditions are impossible. The intended condition should be linear independence/non-parallelism of the vectors, e.g. cross product nonzero or LinearIndependent. Second, the perpendicularity conditions use (a+b) • (c+d) = 0, where • is scalar multiplication (here ring multiplication on ℝ × ℝ), not the Euclidean dot product. The correct condition would be that the inner product/dot product of the two sums is zero. The quantifier and type ℝ × ℝ for plane vectors are appropriate, and the list of pair-sum conditions is redundant but otherwise captures the intended pairings. Because of the incorrect collinearity and dot-product encodings, the statement does not faithfully represent the mathematical problem.",
